-- title:
--   Comparison morphism between two-chart integral models
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j,j'\in F$ nonzero. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(j)=$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $R[j]$ (the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$), and $A_\infty(j)=$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the elements of $F$ integral over $R[j^{-1}]$; `TwoChartIntegralModel R F j` is the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras along the middle chart, `toBase R F j` its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$, and `ιFin R F j`, `ιInf R F j` the canonical morphisms from the spectra of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(j)$, $A_\infty(j)$ into it. Assume: $j'\in A_{\mathrm{fin}}(j)$; $s\in A_\infty(j)$ is of the form $s=1+j^{-1}a$ with $a\in A_\infty(j)$; and for every $y\in A_\infty(j')$ there is $n\in\mathbb N$ with $s^ny\in A_\infty(j)$. Then there exist a morphism of schemes $g\colon$ `TwoChartIntegralModel R F j` $\to$ `TwoChartIntegralModel R F j'`, an $R$-algebra map $\iota_F\colon A_{\mathrm{fin}}(j')\to A_{\mathrm{fin}}(j)$ and an $R$-algebra map $\psi\colon A_\infty(j')\to A_\infty(j)[1/s]$ such that $\iota_F$ is the inclusion inside $F$ ($(\iota_F x)=x$ in $F$ for all $x$); for each $y\in A_\infty(j')$ there are $n$ and $z\in A_\infty(j)$ with $s^ny=z$ in $F$ and $\psi(y)\cdot s^n=z$ in $A_\infty(j)[1/s]$; $g$ followed by `toBase R F j'` equals `toBase R F j`; `ιFin R F j` followed by $g$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_F)$ followed by `ιFin R F j'`; and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation map $A_\infty(j)\to A_\infty(j)[1/s]$ followed by `ιInf R F j` and then $g$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\psi)$ followed by `ιInf R F j'`.
--
--   This is the gluing step comparing the two-chart integral models attached to two generators $j,j'$ of the same ambient field $F$: integrality of $j'$ over $R[j]$ gives the morphism on the finite chart, while the hypothesis on $s$ gives it on the distinguished open $D(s)$ of the pole chart, and the two are matched over the pushout. It is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_iso_of_mem_chartAlgFin_of_forall_exists_mul_mem`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_iso_of_mem_chartAlgFin_of_forall_exists_mul_mem), where the hypotheses hold in both directions and the resulting morphisms are mutually inverse.
